    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for the Austin Waves is anchored by the elite matchup profile of **Kyle Tucker** (78.84), who benefits significantly from a favorable clash against V\u00e1squez and maintains a high floor despite park factors. He is joined in the top tier by **Josh Lowe** (66.88), who is a priority start despite the pending lineup status; his dynamic platoon advantage against Civale creates a massive upside for stolen bases, a critical necessity given our roster construction. **Josh Jung** (66.02) rounds out our premium plays, as his strong BvP history and park factors in today's environment push his efficiency well above the base projection, making him a primary source of power production against the lefty Freeland.\n\nStrategic efficiency mandates a careful approach to our fringe starters. **Sam Antonacci** (59.55) secures his spot as the leadoff man, buoyed by elite xwOBA metrics that allow him to weather a neutral matchup, while **Andy Pages** (64.85) remains a high-value play hitting behind **Kyle Tucker**. Conversely, **Liam Hicks** (29.95) represents our most difficult exclusion; he falls well below the 40-point threshold due to a brutal matchup against Sale and significant negative platoon regression. We are prioritizing the higher ceiling of **Nolan Schanuel** (53.80) in the UTIL slot to preserve our game caps while maintaining a safer floor.\n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the lineup fluidity for **Josh Lowe** and **Nolan Schanuel**; should they shift down in the order or be held out, their value\u2014already throttled by the assumption of a #7 spot\u2014will diminish further. While **Jackson Merrill** (49.49) starts today, his matchup against Ohtani is a genuine warning flag, as the elite SP skill of his opponent severely caps his scoring potential. We continue to monitor the status of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** on the IL, as their return remains essential for recapturing the stolen base and power volume currently missing from our active daily rotation.",
